{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features."}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Plugin Architecture","role":"article"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux’s plugin system is a single protocol ("},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":") with four lifecycle hooks and an ordered registry (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","type":"reference"},{"text":"). All store extensibility flows through this contract. The built-in ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"text":" use it, and so do domain-specific features like killswitch enforcement and paywall management.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"The-Dispatch-Lifecycle","text":"The Dispatch Lifecycle"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every call to ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" drives plugins through a four-phase lifecycle:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["plugins.willReduce(state:action:)      \/\/ 1. Pre-reduce (read-only state)","appReducer.reduce(state:action:...)    \/\/ 2. App reducer runs","pluginEffects = plugins.reduce(...)    \/\/ 3. Plugin reducers run","plugins.afterReduce(state:action:)     \/\/ 4. Post-reduce cleanup"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The generic "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" implements this lifecycle internally. You don’t write "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send()"},{"text":" by hand — ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" handles packing, reducing, plugin hooks, unpacking, and effect dispatch.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A fifth method, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"text":", runs once at shutdown to drain async buffers.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All four hooks have default no-op implementations. Each plugin overrides only what it needs."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Core Middleware vs Domain Plugins","anchor":"Core-Middleware-vs-Domain-Plugins"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin system serves two structurally different roles. Recognizing which one a plugin fills determines where it lives, which hooks it uses, and how it couples to the host app."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Core-Middleware","text":"Core Middleware","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" are "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"action-agnostic infrastructure","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":". They never inspect the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Action","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" type, never dispatch actions, and never return effects. They couple only to the shape of state:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" needs keypaths to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" properties.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" needs ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State: Equatable"},{"text":" so it can snapshot and compare.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because they don’t touch actions, they work with any app that uses Swidux — no wiring required beyond construction."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Domain-Plugins","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Domain Plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Killswitch, parental gate, and paywall plugins are ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"domain-specific modules","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" that ship as separate library targets ("},{"code":"SwiduxKillswitch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"SwiduxParentalGate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). They own their own state slices and action enums, dispatch effects, and must be explicitly wired into the host app’s root types.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each domain plugin stores three wiring pieces:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["private let stateKeyPath: WritableKeyPath<RootState, FeatureState>","private let toRootAction: @Sendable (FeatureAction) -> RootAction","private let extractAction: @Sendable (RootAction) -> FeatureAction?"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The host app provides these at init — the plugin never assumes a specific root type."}]},{"text":"Importing at call sites","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Importing-at-call-sites"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because each domain plugin ships as a "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"separate library target","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":", its state and action types are defined in that module — not in "},{"code":"Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A common convention is to re-export core Swidux from "},{"code":"AppState.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"@_exported import Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", but that re-exports ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"core Swidux only"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":"; it does not re-export the plugin modules."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So any file that reads a plugin-owned slice ("},{"code":"store.analytics.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"store.paywall.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.killswitch.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", …) or dispatches a plugin action (","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"PaywallAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", …) must import that plugin’s module in ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"that","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" file:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"touches "},{"code":"store.analytics.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"AnalyticsAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"code":"import SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"touches ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.paywall.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxPaywall"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"touches only "},{"code":"store.ui","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".ui(...)"},{"type":"text","text":" (app-module types) → nothing extra"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The easy case to forget is a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"View"}]},{"type":"text","text":" that reads the slice for display — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppAction.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" already import the module, but the View is a different file. Without the import you get:"}]},{"syntax":null,"code":["property 'isOptedOut' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxAnalytics'","property 'isPro' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxPaywall'"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is to add "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Swidux<Plugin>"},{"type":"text","text":" to that file."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Comparison","level":3,"text":"Comparison"},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Core Middleware","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Domain Plugins"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Action knowledge"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"None","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Full — extracts and lifts actions","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Lifecycle hooks","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":" only"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns effects"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Yes","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State coupling"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" constraint"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keypath to plugin’s own state slice","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Wiring","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Construction only","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keypath + action lifter + action extractor","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Target","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"text":" library","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Separate library target"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Opt-in"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Instantiate and register"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add state, action case, and register"}]}]]]},{"anchor":"The-Decision-Rule","type":"heading","text":"The Decision Rule","level":2},{"type":"aside","style":"important","name":"Important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Does the middleware need to know your action type? If "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"no","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", it’s core middleware — put it in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" and use "},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". If ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"yes","type":"text"}]},{"text":", it’s a domain plugin — give it its own target and use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"text":"Hook Selection Guide","anchor":"Hook-Selection-Guide","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"willReduce(state:action:)","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"text":" — Capture state ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}]},{"text":" the reducer mutates it. State is read-only. Use for snapshots (undo) or pre-mutation analytics.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce(state:action:) -> Effect?"}]},{"text":" — Handle domain-specific actions ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the app reducer. Mutate the plugin’s state slice and return effects. This is the only hook that can dispatch actions or do async work."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce(state:action:)"}]},{"text":" — Observe state ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" all reducing is done. Use for persistence draining, logging, or metrics. Cannot return effects."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush() async"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Shutdown hook. Flush pending async buffers (persistence writes, analytics batches). Called once when the app exits."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Registration-Order","text":"Registration Order","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" executes plugins in registration order. Recommended ordering:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. Must snapshot before any mutation","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. Drains changelogs after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. Domain plugins in any order","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Undo must come first — it snapshots state in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"text":", before the app reducer or any plugin modifies it. Persistence typically comes next so its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"text":" drain sees the final state. Domain plugins use only ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"text":", so their relative order rarely matters.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Service-Result Actions and Transition Observation","anchor":"Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"service-result action"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerInfoUpdated"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KillswitchPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verdictReceived"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshSucceeded"},{"type":"text","text":" — fires on "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"every","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" fetch, refresh, or stream tick, not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"only when the value changed, and unconditionally writes its payload to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state slice. The payload is frequently identical to what is already there","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(a re-delivered entitlement, an unchanged remote config).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Do "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" map analytics or side effects to the raw service-result action:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it fires duplicates by design. Observe the "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state slice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — or a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"derived from it — instead.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State observation is already deduplicated by the framework. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"packs the observer into a value-type snapshot, lets reducers mutate the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"snapshot, then writes back via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State.apply"},{"type":"text","text":". For a leaf slice that write"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a plain assignment whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" setter equality-gates "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values, so a slice whose value did not change emits no notification — and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value-diffing consumer such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsIdentity.userProperties"},{"type":"text","text":" (which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" re-evaluates and diffs every non-analytics dispatch) sees exactly the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"real transitions. This dedup is a property of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":", not of any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per-plugin guard, so a no-op service-result cycle is silent to state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observers without any extra reducer logic."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Next Steps","anchor":"Next-Steps","level":2},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — Step-by-step guide to creating a domain plugin"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — Configure the built-in persistence middleware"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — Add undo\/redo with the built-in undo middleware"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Explanation","anchor":"Explanation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"],"generated":true}],"kind":"article","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","type":"topic","title":"Architecture & Performance","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SecurityPosture":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"What Swidux’s soft controls actually guarantee, and what to do when you need a hard one.","type":"text"}],"role":"collectionGroup","type":"topic","title":"Security Posture","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/securityposture","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store":{"title":"Store","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Store"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Store"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Generic store that owns the dispatch cycle, plugin lifecycle, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observation layer."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"role":"collection","title":"Swidux","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidu